# Section Components and Page Layout Guidelines

This guide outlines the conventions for creating section components and page layouts throughout the application.

## Section Types

Our codebase includes several main section component types:

- **Hero Sections**: [Hero.js](mdc:components/Hero.js) introduces the main product
- **Feature Sections**: Several variations ([FeaturesAccordion.js](mdc:components/FeaturesAccordion.js), [FeaturesGrid.js](mdc:components/FeaturesGrid.js), [FeaturesListicle.js](mdc:components/FeaturesListicle.js))
- **CTA Sections**: [CTA.js](mdc:components/CTA.js) for call-to-action
- **Pricing Sections**: [Pricing.js](mdc:components/Pricing.js) displays product plans
- **Testimonial Sections**: Various testimonial components showing social proof
- **FAQ Sections**: [FAQ.js](mdc:components/FAQ.js) for frequently asked questions
- **Problem Sections**: [Problem.js](mdc:components/Problem.js) for problem statement/agitation

## Section Structure

- **Container Pattern**
  - Use `max-w-*` Tailwind classes to constrain width
  - Center with `mx-auto`
  - Add appropriate padding with `px-8` or similar
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use container pattern
  <section className="bg-base-100">
    <div className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-8 py-24">
      {/* Section content */}
    </div>
  </section>
  ```

- **Section Spacing**
  - Standard vertical spacing: `py-24` or `py-16 md:py-24`
  - Adjust for responsive layouts with breakpoint-specific classes
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use consistent vertical spacing
  <section className="py-16 md:py-24 lg:py-32">
    {/* Section content */}
  </section>
  ```

## Section Component Organization

- **Section Components as Default Exports**
  - Each major section should be its own component
  - Export as the default from its file
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Create standalone section components
  const FeaturesSection = () => {
    return (
      <section className="bg-base-200">
        {/* Section content */}
      </section>
    );
  };
  
  export default FeaturesSection;
  ```

- **Subcomponents Within Sections**
  - Define child components within the same file
  - Keep these as function components above the main component
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Define subcomponents within section files
  // Subcomponent
  const FeatureCard = ({ title, description, icon }) => {
    return (
      <div className="card">
        {icon}
        <h3>{title}</h3>
        <p>{description}</p>
      </div>
    );
  };
  
  // Main section component
  const FeaturesSection = () => {
    return (
      <section>
        <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
          <FeatureCard 
            title="Feature 1"
            description="Description"
            icon={<SomeIcon />}
          />
          {/* More feature cards */}
        </div>
      </section>
    );
  };
  ```

## Page Layout Structure

- **Page Component Pattern**
  - Pages assembled from section components
  - Each page is a server component by default
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Compose pages from section components
  export default function HomePage() {
    return (
      <>
        <Hero />
        <FeaturesSection />
        <Pricing />
        <FAQ />
        <CTA />
      </>
    );
  }
  ```

- **Layout Structure**
  - Use Next.js layout components for shared UI
  - Keep headers, footers in layout, not individual pages
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use layout components for shared UI
  export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
    return (
      <html lang="en">
        <body>
          <Header />
          <main>{children}</main>
          <Footer />
        </body>
      </html>
    );
  }
  ```

## Responsive Layout Patterns

- **Mobile-First Approach**
  - Design for mobile first, then enhance for larger screens
  - Use Tailwind responsive classes (md:, lg:, etc.) to adapt layouts
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use responsive classes for layout changes
  <div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4 md:gap-8">
    <div className="w-full md:w-1/2">
      {/* First column */}
    </div>
    <div className="w-full md:w-1/2">
      {/* Second column */}
    </div>
  </div>
  ```

- **Responsive Grid System**
  - Use CSS Grid with responsive columns
  - Adjust column count at different breakpoints
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use responsive grid layouts
  <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
    {/* Grid items */}
  </div>
  ```

## Section Typography

- **Heading Hierarchy**
  - Use appropriate heading levels (h1, h2, h3)
  - Consistent font weights: `font-bold` or `font-extrabold` for headings
  - Consistent sizing scale using Tailwind text classes
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use consistent heading hierarchy
  <section>
    <h2 className="font-extrabold text-3xl lg:text-5xl tracking-tight mb-8">
      Section Heading
    </h2>
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
      <div>
        <h3 className="font-bold text-xl mb-4">Subsection Heading</h3>
        <p className="text-base-content/80">Description text</p>
      </div>
      {/* More items */}
    </div>
  </section>
  ```

- **Text Formatting**
  - Body text: Standard size with reduced opacity for secondary text
  - Use `tracking-tight` for headings
  - Use `leading-relaxed` for paragraph text
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use consistent text formatting
  <p className="text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
    Paragraph text with appropriate line height and reduced opacity
  </p>
  ```

## Color and Background

- **Section Background Alternation**
  - Alternate between `bg-base-100` and `bg-base-200` for visual separation
  - Use `bg-neutral` with `text-neutral-content` for high-contrast sections
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Alternate section backgrounds
  <section className="bg-base-100">
    {/* Section content */}
  </section>
  <section className="bg-base-200">
    {/* Next section content */}
  </section>
  <section className="bg-neutral text-neutral-content">
    {/* High-contrast section */}
  </section>
  ```

- **DaisyUI Theme Integration**
  - Use theme-aware colors: `primary`, `secondary`, `accent`, etc.
  - Use opacity modifiers for subtle variations: `bg-primary/20`
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use theme-aware colors
  <div className="bg-primary/20 text-primary rounded-lg p-4">
    {/* Themed content */}
  </div>
  ```

## Section Animation and Interactivity

- **Animate on Interaction**
  - Use Tailwind's transition utilities for interactive elements
  - Keep animations subtle and purposeful
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use subtle animations
  <button className="transition-all duration-200 hover:scale-105">
    Interactive Element
  </button>
  ```

- **Section-Specific Interactivity**
  - Interactive elements should be client components
  - Keep state management clean with React hooks
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Implement clean interactivity
  "use client";
  
  import { useState } from "react";
  
  const TabSection = () => {
    const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState(0);
    
    return (
      <section>
        <div className="tabs">
          {tabData.map((tab, i) => (
            <button 
              key={i}
              className={`tab ${activeTab === i ? 'tab-active' : ''}`}
              onClick={() => setActiveTab(i)}
            >
              {tab.title}
            </button>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div className="tab-content">
          {tabData[activeTab].content}
        </div>
      </section>
    );
  };
  ```

## Semantic HTML Structure

- **HTML5 Semantic Elements**
  - Use `<section>` for distinct content sections
  - Use `<header>` and `<footer>` appropriately
  - Use `<nav>` for navigation areas
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use semantic HTML elements
  <section aria-labelledby="features-heading">
    <header>
      <h2 id="features-heading">Features</h2>
    </header>
    <div className="content">
      {/* Features content */}
    </div>
  </section>
  ```

## Page SEO Optimization

- **Section IDs for Navigation**
  - Add IDs to main sections for anchor links
  - Use descriptive IDs that match content
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Add section IDs for navigation
  <section id="pricing" className="bg-base-200">
    <h2>Pricing Plans</h2>
    {/* Pricing content */}
  </section>
  ```

- **Content Structure**
  - Organize content in a logical hierarchy
  - Use appropriate heading levels (h1-h6)
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Use proper content hierarchy
  <article>
    <h1>Main Page Title</h1>
    <section>
      <h2>Major Section</h2>
      <div>
        <h3>Subsection</h3>
        <p>Content</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
  ```

## Performance Considerations

- **Lazy Loading Sections**
  - Consider lazy loading below-the-fold sections
  - Use Next.js `<Suspense>` for progressive loading
  
  ```javascript
  // ✅ DO: Lazy load below-the-fold content
  import { Suspense } from 'react';
  const LowerSection = dynamic(() => import('./LowerSection'));
  
  // In the page component:
  <Suspense fallback={<div className="h-96 skeleton"></div>}>
    <LowerSection />
  </Suspense>
  ```

These guidelines ensure consistent section implementation and page layout throughout the application, improving user experience, SEO, and maintainability.
